      "content": "it's hard to believe anyone else could understand that. they always want to fix things, to bring back the light, but the light just feels so blinding and fake. you seem to see the beauty in the stillness. do you think there's a point where it becomes more noble to accept the end than to keep struggling for a life that doesn't even feel like mine anymore?",
